<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:c="using:JustPlay.UI.Controls"
             x:Class="JustPlay.UI.Controls.BusyOverlay"
             IsHitTestVisible="False">

    <!--
      Shared J.U.S.T. progress overlay — a floating card in a card's OVERLAY layer, so showing
      progress NEVER reflows the layout (Chloe 2026-07-15: an inline progress bar "schiebt unten
      alles rechts raus - das ist schlechtes design. können wir kein generelles overlay basteln was
      wir überall nutzen können?"). Drop it as the LAST child of a card's Panel, bind IsActive to a
      busy flag, Message to a status line and (optionally) Progress to a 0..1 value. It is
      IsHitTestVisible=False — purely visual, it never eats a click on the controls underneath.

      0.6 rebuild (Chloe 2026-07-30: "ich mag die progress anzeige überhaupt nicht .. zuckelt zum
      wenn sich der text ändert (es er ständig tut) die bar ist viel zu schmal … ich hätte lieber
      was rundes modernes schickes"):

        · ROUND. A hand-drawn ProgressRing replaces the 74×3 px bar, with the percentage inside it.
        · IT CANNOT JITTER. The card has a FIXED width and the text is centred inside it, so a
          message changing per file no longer shoves the whole pill sideways. The old one was
          centre-aligned with automatic width — every new string re-measured and moved it.
        · The ring's value EASES toward its target (see ProgressRing), so per-file reporting reads
          as one smooth sweep instead of a stutter.

      Anti-flicker is unchanged: nothing appears before ShowDelayMs of continuous busy, so the fast
      per-knob re-renders that make a lab feel instant never flash a spinner. The look is the shared
      themed card (BgLinear/BgGlowA + hairline + soft shadow), so it tracks the live theme.
    -->
    <Panel>
        <Border x:Name="Pill" IsVisible="False"
                Width="248"
                HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Bottom"
                Margin="0,0,0,20" CornerRadius="16" ClipToBounds="True"
                BoxShadow="0 12 34 0 #A6000000">
            <Panel>
                <Rectangle Fill="{DynamicResource BgLinear}" RadiusX="16" RadiusY="16"/>
                <Rectangle Fill="{DynamicResource BgGlowA}"  RadiusX="16" RadiusY="16"/>
                <Border BorderBrush="#26FFFFFF" BorderThickness="1" CornerRadius="16"/>

                <StackPanel Margin="18,16" Spacing="11" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch">
                    <c:ProgressRing x:Name="Ring"
                                    Width="52" Height="52"
                                    HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                    RingThickness="4"
                                    Progress="{Binding $parent[c:BusyOverlay].Progress}"
                                    TrackBrush="#1FFFFFFF"
                                    ArcBrush="{DynamicResource AccentGradient}"
                                    LabelBrush="#E6FFFFFF"/>

                    <!-- Fixed height + centred: the phase line changes a handful of times per job
                         and must not resize the card when it does. -->
                    <TextBlock x:Name="MsgText" FontSize="12.5" Height="17"
                               HorizontalAlignment="Center" TextAlignment="Center"
                               Foreground="#E6FFFFFF" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                               Text="{Binding $parent[c:BusyOverlay].Message}"/>

                    <!-- The counter that used to churn the layout. Same fixed-height treatment, and
                         it collapses to nothing when a job has no detail to report. -->
                    <TextBlock x:Name="DetailText" FontSize="10.5" Height="14"
                               HorizontalAlignment="Center" TextAlignment="Center"
                               Foreground="#8CFFFFFF" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                               Text="{Binding $parent[c:BusyOverlay].Detail}"
                               IsVisible="{Binding $parent[c:BusyOverlay].Detail,
                                                   Converter={x:Static StringConverters.IsNotNullOrEmpty}}"/>
                </StackPanel>
            </Panel>
        </Border>
    </Panel>
</UserControl>
